ontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-02T10:20:00Z","updated_at":"2025-12-02T10:20:00Z","body":"This introduced a regression causing crashes if the editor selection is changed while looping over the List<>& reference of `EditorSelection::top_selected_node_list`\r\n\r\nOne reliable way to reproduce this is the \"Change Type\" operation in a scene node's context menu, since this will change the type of the selected node while iterating over the selection.\r\n\r\nThe first iteration of the loop will run fine, but the for loop may attempt another loop iteration given that the selection list state has already been corrupted by the end of the for block.\r\n<img width=\"1798\" height=\"1377\" alt=\"code block for SceneTreeDock::_create (current_option == TOOL_REPLACE)\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d5445f3d-ca68-44ea-97d7-19fe6ab1036e\" />\r\n\r\nI haven't 100% verified that this is the regression, but I believe it is correct to make a copy of the selection list while performing a dangerous operation (also includes anything that could possibly trigger a signal or call into script), and the code prior to this PR was making a copy of the list.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"